[h1]S3GM: Skate 3 in Gmod[/h1]
Skate 3's real skating in Garry's Mod: its own physics, flick-it tricks, grinds, manuals, bails and the mach 1 glitch, running on the community's Skate 3 engine rewrite. Works on any map (grind rails are found automatically) with any playermodel, big or small. Equip the Skateboard and you're riding.

[b]Free forever.[/b] Unofficial fan project, not affiliated with EA or Facepunch.

[h2]Download and updates[/h2]
[b]Updates and downloads live on GitHub now:[/b]
[url=https://github.com/NotEnxvinity/skate3-gmod/releases]github.com/NotEnxvinity/skate3-gmod/releases[/url] (Windows / Linux / SteamOS and Mac zips, plus the source)
Source code (GPL-3.0) and bug reports: [url=https://github.com/NotEnxvinity/skate3-gmod]github.com/NotEnxvinity/skate3-gmod[/url]
[b]Setup video:[/b] [url=https://youtu.be/oGdIwMNwp14]https://youtu.be/oGdIwMNwp14[/url]
Discord: Enxvinity's Atelier, channel gmod-releases.

[h2]What's new in v2.3.1[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Chibi and giant playermodels[/b]: the skater and board scale to the model, so small models no longer float above the board. [b]skate3_scale_to_model 0[/b] turns it off.
[*][b]Hall of Meat is on by default[/b] for new installs (Spawn menu > Utilities > Skate 3 to turn it off).
[*]With Hall of Meat off, a bail no longer flashes "Bailed" in the score.
[*]Windows setup copes with a broken or leftover Python ("No module named encodings").
[/list]

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*]Skate 3's physics and trick system, driven from a controller like the real thing.
[*]Your own playermodel rides the board, posed by Skate 3's animations, and other players see you skate.
[*]Skate 3's own sound engine (beta), ported from becaring/SK8V and fed from your disc: pops and landings by surface, grind and wheel loops, seam clicks, bails and the real x2/x3 chimes, quieter and panned when they're far from you, with echo in reverb areas. The older Skate 3 sounds (or Half-Life 2's) are the fallback.
[*]Skate 3's HUD and menus: score, LINE, trick stack, FAKIE, the Hall of Meat bail panel, and the L1 quick menu (session marker, Interact, games).
[*]Seven skatepark maps (gm_skate3_*) that build their parks from your disc when you load them, plus tool gun placement for park pieces.
[*]Skaters hit each other: crashes, punches and board smacks (B / R1). Spawned props you don't freeze can be skated too.
[*]Trick score in three styles: minimal, floating beside you, or Half-Life 2.
[*]Session markers, like Skate 3. Bail damage can be switched off by the server.
[*]The [b]Skate 3 Surface[/b] tool (tool gun, Skate 3 tab) fixes a map's collision for skating: flatten a bumpy floor, smooth a ramp, ignore clutter, draw a grind rail, or make a ramp prop use its visible shape. Flags are saved per map and can be shared as a file.
[/list]

[h2]What you need[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Your own copy of Skate 3 for Xbox 360, as a disc image (.iso).[/b] Nothing from EA's game ships here, ever. The setup reads what the mod needs from your disc on your own computer.
[*]64-bit Garry's Mod: Steam > Garry's Mod > Properties > Betas > [b]x86-64[/b].
[*]Linux / SteamOS (native or Proton), Windows, or a Mac (tested on Apple silicon). Use the GitHub download for your computer.
[*]A controller is recommended. Keyboard and mouse is early and experimental. On Steam Deck / SteamOS, Garry's Mod's controller layout must be a [b]Gamepad[/b] template, not keyboard and mouse.
[/list]

[h2]Install[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Subscribe to this addon.
[*]Download the zip for your computer from [url=https://github.com/NotEnxvinity/skate3-gmod/releases]GitHub Releases[/url] and [b]extract it anywhere[/b]. You get one folder: S3GM-setup. The Workshop can't carry the skate engine itself, so it comes from there, like G64 does.
[*]Double-click the setup: [b]S3GM-setup-Windows.bat[/b] (Windows), [b]S3GM-setup-Linux.sh[/b] (Linux / SteamOS, pick Execute) or [b]S3GM-setup-Mac.command[/b] (Mac; if macOS blocks it: Privacy & Security > Open Anyway).
[*]Check your [b]garrysmod[/b] folder (lowercase, inside GarrysMod) and your Skate 3 .iso, press Install. Leave "Skate 3's own sound engine" ticked (a few GB, a few more minutes). Updating? Run the new setup again.
[*]Wait for "All set!", load a map and equip [b]Skateboard[/b] (spawn menu > Weapons > Skate 3).
[/olist]

[h2]Controls[/h2]
Skate 3's own: [b]A[/b] pushes, [b]Y[/b] gets on and off the board, the right stick flicks tricks, triggers grab. [b]D-pad down[/b] drops a session marker, hold [b]D-pad up[/b] to go back to it. [b]B[/b] / [b]R1[/b] punches, or smacks with the board when it's in your hand. Switch weapons to leave skate mode.

[h2]Settings[/h2]
Spawn menu > Utilities > Skate 3: stance (regular or goofy), camera height, the sound engine switch with its status, Hall of Meat, volume, and the trick score's look. Server: [b]skate3_bail_damage[/b] turns bail damage on or off.

[h2]Uninstall[/h2]
Close Garry's Mod first. [b]Never delete the whole garrysmod folder[/b], other addons live in it. Delete only these S3GM folders and files inside your garrysmod folder: addons/skate3, data/skate3 (the big one), sound/skate3, materials/skate3, resource/fonts/s3gm_futura.ttf, and gmcl_skate3_*.dll in lua/bin. On Windows also delete %LOCALAPPDATA%\skate3-gmod. Then unsubscribe here.
Linux / SteamOS / Mac: set G to your garrysmod folder, then run:
[code]rm -rf ~/.cache/skate3-gmod "$G/addons/skate3" "$G/data/skate3" "$G/sound/skate3" "$G/materials/skate3" "$G/resource/fonts/s3gm_futura.ttf" "$G"/lua/bin/gmcl_skate3_*.dll[/code]

[h2]Known conflicts[/h2]
These addons together leaked memory until the game crashed during testing. If you see "CUtlRBTree overflow", try disabling them:
[list]
[*]First-person body ("Тело от Первого лица")
[*]Source Shadows
[*]InfMap base
[*]LIDAR
[*]Portal Gun (Lua rework)
[*]"better'er grab!" and SkateGM (skategm_* files) don't work alongside S3GM
[/list]

